    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 174\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 9425, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT authorizing the commissioner of general services to transfer\n      and  convey  certain  unappropriated  state  land to the Sing Sing\n      Prison Museum, county of Westchester\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This legislation would allow the Sing  Sing  Prison  Museum  to  lease\ncertain  lands  within the Sing Sing Correctional Facility, specifically\nincluding that which contains the former Powerhouse, for the purposes of\nestablishing a museum.\n \n  The Sing Sing Prison Museum group is still  approximately  five  years\nfrom  being  able to financially afford to lease the location. The group\nremains in conversations with the Office of  General  Services  and  the\nDepartment  of Corrections and Community Supervision about being granted\nan easement to the cell block for visitors to see. Given that the  ease-\nment  can  be  granted  without  legislation and that authorization of a\nlease is premature, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
    "vetoNumber": 174,
